{"id": "unknown-2026-09-11-010", "date": "2026-09-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["green_hydrogen_cost", "electrolyzer_capacity"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "The Hydrogen Stream: AEM electrolysis could deliver hydrogen at $3.27/kg, say Repsol, P2HP", "content": "<p>Power to Hydrogen (P2H2) and Repsol completed a 1,250-hour pilot of P2H2’s hybrid AEM electrolyzer technology, demonstrating operation at 40% to 100% load, pressures up to 30 bar and hydrogen purity of up to 99.9%. P2H2 projects an LCOH of €3.86 ($4.47)/kg, potentially falling to €2.82/kg under optimized renewable energy conditions, and the companies are considering a 500 kW-to-MW-scale demonstration.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/11/the-hydrogen-stream-aem-elec", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/11/the-hydrogen-stream-aem-electrolysis-could-deliver-hydrogen-at-3-27-kg-say-repsol-p2hp/", "type": "rss"}]}
